  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "$\\frac{4}{9}\\times 54=$",
  "worked_solution": "Interpreting the fraction as division, we can write our expression as:\n\n$$\n4÷9\\times 54\n$$\n\nWe can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷9$ and the $\\times 54:$\n\n$$\n4\\times 54÷9\n$$\n\nExpressing the division as a fraction, we arrive at:\n\n$$\n4\\times \\frac{54}{9}\n$$\n\nWe now solve:\n\n$$\n4\\times {{\\frac{54}{9}}_{⏟}}_{6}=4\\times 6=24\n$$",
